TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC -- not for merging.

The rear camera on this board does not answer at the OV13B10 address
(0x36); the gaokun3 board ships more than one rear module. To find out what
is actually on the rear CCI bus, scan it from ov13b10_probe() while the
rails and MCLK are still up: the sensor only answers when powered, and
neither the regulators nor MCLK4 can be driven from userspace on this
kernel (the clk_prepare_enable debugfs file is behind
CLOCK_ALLOW_WRITE_DEBUGFS, which the kernel config leaves off).

Every address in 0x08..0x77 that ACKs is logged as
    ov13b10 1-0036: cci scan: 0xNN ACKs

Remove this patch once the rear module has been identified.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c	2026-09-29 20:41:59.917633161 +0800
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c	2026-09-29 20:41:59.917633161 +0800
@@ -1695,6 +1695,22 @@
 		ret = ov13b10_identify_module(ov13b);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(ov13b->dev, "failed to find sensor: %d\n", ret);
+			{
+				int a;
+
+				for (a = 0x08; a < 0x78; a++) {
+					u8 b;
+					struct i2c_msg msg = {
+						.addr = a,
+						.flags = I2C_M_RD,
+						.len = 1,
+						.buf = &b,
+					};
+
+					if (i2c_transfer(client->adapter, &msg, 1) == 1)
+						dev_info(ov13b->dev, "cci scan: 0x%02x ACKs\n", a);
+				}
+			}
 			goto error_power_off;
 		}
 	}
